# Resolve a concurrent append to the decision log by keeping both sides rather than
# conflicting. WHERE THIS APPLIES IS NOT OBVIOUS AND IS MEASURED IN docs/DECISIONS.md:
# git reads this file from the tree of the checkout PERFORMING the merge, so it applies
# only when that checkout's tree carries this line. NO LANDING HAS IT: the repository is
# squash-only, so a pull request reaches main as a forge-authored commit and the forge
# does not honour merge=union. It can only apply to a LOCAL merge before landing -- an
# author syncing, or an operator's trial merge -- and a branch cut before this line
# landed has neither. The structural guard that pairs with it is
# scripts/check-decision-log.mjs.
docs/DECISIONS.md merge=union
